WEBVTT

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:20.010
Rental Magica

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.960
I knew it! A mistake!

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:46.860
Rejected!

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:49.560
Now!

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:05.080
Um, everyone? Um...

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:08.020
So, this is what it's like to be
so dizzy, your head spins.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.390
Well, it's December.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:10.880
December! December!

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.080
Excuse me.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:14.820
Oh, Kuroha.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.590
Could you move, please?

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.600
Oh! Sure.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.810
Everyone looks busy.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.270
So, what should I do?

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.740
Episode 12
CHRISTMAS EVE REQUIEM

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.670
Honami! Honami!

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:05.300
Huh?

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.910
You're just standing around fidgeting,
and you seem like you're in a daze.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.290
Something on your mind?

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.780
N-Not really.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:15.920
Christmas Eve, right?

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.060
W-What's with that knowing laugh of yours?!

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:28.570
Hello, you two. Sorry for not keeping in touch.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.090
Diana?!
Diana?!

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.240
I brought your usual order,

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:36.300
along with a few things I thought you'd
need for the New Year's ceremonies.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:39.980
Plus, I came to thank you for
your continuing patronage.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:41.770
Thank you.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:45.550
Unfortunately, the president's out now. Sorry.

00:03:45.890 --> 00:03:50.380
Oh, no. I already gave him my greeting.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:53.720
He paid me a visit the other day.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.130
D-Did he do something?

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:58.130
Oh no, no.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:03.470
When he came to me directly, I thought he
might have an urgent request, but actually...

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:09.140
What kind of presents do girls like?

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:12.100
...is what he asked me.

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.710
F-For who?! For who?!

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.520
Miss Adelicia...

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.650
Miss Adelicia...

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.550
Miss Adelicia!

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:31.790
In the last three days,
you have sighed 47 times, Miss Adelicia.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.930
You have stared off into space while
not astral projecting 28 times.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.570
And you've meaninglessly wandered
around your study 34 times.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.340
T-That's how much I usually do that!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.540
You're also holding that grimoire upside-down.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:47.370
I... I knew that!

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:53.780
I just thought I'd give myself a handicap
because it's boring to read it the usual way.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.110
Of course.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:00.930
However, everyone in Goetia is busy preparing
for the annual winter solstice ceremony.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:05.770
They ask that you please pay a bit
more attention to that, Miss Adelicia.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.460
Of course!

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.030
It's just, I've sort of been thinking about Itsuki...

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:12.400
Master Itsuki?

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:13.980
Now that you mention it,

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:18.780
he came to me the other day and
asked me a most mysterious question...

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:20.840
W-What was it?!

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.580
It seemed very difficult for him to ask.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.080
What do you wish of me?

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:30.480
What kind of presents do girls like?

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:31.750
...he said.

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:32.920
What?!

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:36.060
F-F-For who?!

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.040
Addie?

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.370
What are you doing here?

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.670
Where are you going, Honami?

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:57.080
Well, I have some business with our president.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.120
I also have business with him.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:00.820
Crap!

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:04.350
If I don't hurry, I won't get the present in time!

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:08.460
Present...

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.090
Present...

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.230
Could it be for me?
Could it be for me?

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.830
Wha? Shinogi's shrine?

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.510
Why would Itsuki come here?

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:21.340
Well, well, look who's here.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:25.770
A Celtic witch and a princess of
Solomon. A rare combination.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.740
Miss Shinogi! So, how did
things turn out for you?

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:33.210
Thanks to you, my brother has recovered.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.920
He even told the doctor he
doesn't need any more rehab.

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.890
Well, speak of the devil.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.050
Moroha!

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.400
Well, well... We haven't spoken in a while.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:46.220
I owe you much for the service you performed.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.770
The blood of Minagi will not
forget the debt it owes Astral.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:51.400
You're welcome here any time.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.940
You're looking well, Moroha.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:54.770
Well...

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:59.340
He's living like he's making up
for being asleep for 10 years.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.470
Look over there.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:05.790
My... You don't often see a
Christmas tree at a shrine.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:08.990
A lot of parishioners visit the
shrine at this time of the year,

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.590
so I thought I'd decorate it as part of
the festivities at the end of the month.

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:15.360
He's a priest with the heart of a businessman!

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.640
Well, that isn't far off from
the meaning of Christmas...

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.630
C-Come to think of it, where's Itsuki?

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.730
Have you seen our president?

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:28.700
Oh, I just paid him for the
part-time work he's been doing.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:31.380
He's been doing some work
here for the last few days.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.610
D-Do you know the reason why?

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:42.450
I think he mentioned that he wants
to buy a Christmas present.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.230
D... Did he say anything besides that?

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:48.290
If you mean who he's buying it for, then...

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.460
It's for someone very special.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:53.070
S-Someone very special?!
S-Someone very special?!

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:56.130
Itsuki ran off in a big hurry.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:59.300
He left through the rear gate a little while ago.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.200
E-Excuse us!
E-Excuse us!

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:20.960
No good.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.820
He isn't here.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:28.190
Even if I try dowsing, I'm worried
he'd trace the spell power back to me.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:33.230
That eye of his means he can find you
if you just get into his field of vision.

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:34.970
I can't believe we can't use magic.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.310
Amazing. Icchan is usually
so clueless, and now...

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:39.940
Somebody call my name?

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:41.840
I... Icchan!

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.910
Itsuki! How long have you been there?!

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:45.850
I just went down the wrong street.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:50.280
Look, there's something I want to ask you, Boss.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:51.320
Yeah?

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.430
It's about... Uh...

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.490
Y... Y... Y...

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.830
You copied your homework from
Yamada in our class, right?!

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:03.070
You have to do your own schoolwork!

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:05.170
Uh, s-sorry!

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:09.710
Itsuki! There's something I want to ask you, too!

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:11.910
I... I... I...

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:16.080
In 400 words or less, what are
the magical roots of Christmas?!

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:18.340
Um... Uh...

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:24.220
What we call Christmas was the period when
the Roman god Saturnus would revive.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.660
Also when the Persian god Mithras would revive.

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:30.660
Sorry, I haven't studied enough!

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:34.040
Boss, what I really wanted to ask was-

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:38.800
The tradition of giving presents comes
from the legend of St. Nicholas, so...

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:43.110
Addie, don't force him!

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:44.900
What about you, Honami?!

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.910
I'll be sure to study next time.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.380
Anyway, I have an appointment, so gotta run!

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:01.660
Appointment?
Appointment?

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:13.130
Who would he be meeting on Christmas Eve?

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:15.670
The one he's giving the present to?

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:38.390
Let's go.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:45.390
What's going on here?

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:47.970
And who's that girl?

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.760
Typical Itsuki.

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:15.130
Really.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.240
Even though it's not a job...

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:20.570
He's buying a present for a little ghost girl.

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:24.240
Hey, where's Big Sister Honami?

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:26.350
She's late.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:29.150
I wonder what's keeping her.

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.320
It's not fair, her ducking out of work!

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:35.320
I'll go see what's up.

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:51.470
There she is! Honami, I came to find you!

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:54.940
Oh, Adelicia. Is something up?

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:00.040
Oh?

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:02.970
There's more to this story, it seems.

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.310
Where are they going?

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.160
What is this spell power I sense?

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:15.230
There shouldn't be a church out here.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.800
This should be vacant land.

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:20.390
Then, this is...

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:36.070
Honami, this church and those dead spirits!

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.680
Spell wave contamination that's
specifically linked to Christmas Eve!

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.420
What do you mean?

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:44.390
There are types of spell wave contamination...

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:47.220
...that are only triggered
under specific conditions.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:49.660
Like haunted promontories and will o' wisps.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:53.330
This church and those spirits only
appear on Christmas Eve.

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:55.730
Then, Itsuki is...

00:12:57.770 --> 00:13:01.570
Come forth, Forneus!
The marquis who rules 29 legions!

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:11.450
Itsuki!

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:12.150
Icchan!

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:13.080
Itsuki!

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:19.520
Huh? What are you all doing here?

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:25.120
I... Itsuki! What's going on here?!

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:30.700
Could you please explain?

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:35.140
It was about a week ago...

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:39.710
I saw this girl in town and
just couldn't ignore her.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.180
And I called out to her.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.550
Come on, big sale!

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:49.720
Big sale, here! Everything, 30% off! Big sale!

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:55.120
Ho! Ho! Ho! Presents from Santa!

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:56.530
What's wrong?

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:02.170
You see... You see... Santa!

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.530
I figured she wanted a present.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.040
That she was trying to say
"Please give me something."

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:09.940
But it looks like I was wrong.

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:12.780
And then there are these friends of hers, too.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.150
Ghosts don't need physical things.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:19.010
She must want something else.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:30.260
Dear Lord, we thank you for
this bounty we receive tonight.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:34.330
In your name, we pray. Amen.

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:35.500
Amen.

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:42.470
There, you've chopped enough for tonight.

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:44.130
Let's head inside.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.910
Tonight's Christmas Eve.

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:50.840
You have to hang up your
stockings in your room.

00:15:02.930 --> 00:15:04.920
Good night, Father.

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:06.860
Santa...

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.260
Merry Christmas.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:11.170
Santa...

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:38.860
Only those feelings remain here.

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:44.200
And that sadness triggers the spell wave
contamination only on Christmas Eve.

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.000
Jeez, Boss...

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:48.810
Why didn't you come to us
about this in the first place?

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:49.770
I'm sorry.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:54.010
I would have consulted you,
but everyone was so busy.

00:15:55.250 --> 00:15:58.480
Well, even saying that,
there's nothing we can do about this.

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:02.350
I know!

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:05.850
Isn't there some sort of magic
that can be made into a present?

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:09.690
The right sort of magic that would
calm a heart on Christmas Eve?

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:12.490
Magic as a present?

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:16.200
Itsuki, what do you think
we are, stage magicians?!

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:18.170
Oh, I guess not...

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:19.560
Something fun.

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:21.910
Magic to make their hearts dance.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.240
Like, maybe...

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:28.200
A song?

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:31.350
A song... A song?

00:16:32.690 --> 00:16:33.210
A song!

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:38.620
Is that... a no?

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:48.100
Running through the white snow,

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:52.660
hearing the bells ringing out.

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:58.910
Over fields, through the woods we go.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:01.380
W-Why do we have to do this?!
Over fields, through the woods we go.

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.420
Forget it. I'm not doing
something this embarrassing.
Over fields, through the woods we go.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:03.910
Forget it. I'm not doing
something this embarrassing.

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:15.060
On this holy night, let's make a wish on a star.

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:21.440
So, let's sing a happy song tonight...

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:26.300
...as the stars shine.

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:31.840
The happy sound of bells nearby.

00:17:32.180 --> 00:17:37.170
Making a wreath out of holly.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:42.790
So, let's sing a happy song tonight...

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:47.490
...as the the stars shine.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:53.200
The saint draws near.

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:58.560
Let's decorate the fir tree.

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:06.340
Fill our stockings with dreams
as we drift off to sleep.

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:09.550
Giving a song as a present...

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:10.780
That's so like Itsuki!

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:15.350
They once called Santa Claus a heretic.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:17.920
We're not doing anything wrong.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.490
I'm gonna make you pay for this later, Itsuki.

00:18:31.870 --> 00:18:37.410
So, let's all sing a song tonight...

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:42.470
...to echo into the night sky.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:47.890
Santa is singing this song, too.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:53.150
Turn your laughter into its melody.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:58.320
So, let's sing a song together tonight...

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:03.630
...to echo into the snow as it falls.

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:09.070
Let our voices mix together and spread.

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:14.470
Let the spirit of thanks into your heart.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:22.590
And pray that we pass this day with a smile.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.570
I just remembered.

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:48.180
Christmas was originally a festival for giving
gifts to the dead who return to earth.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:51.610
Hm?

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:54.380
A doll.

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:59.660
That priest was probably going to play Santa
and hide it in one of the children's stockings.

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:01.180
A Christmas present...

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:04.720
This was the core of the
spell wave contamination.

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:23.410
A Christmas present from Heaven, you think?

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:32.860
Huh? Nobody's around?

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:33.730
Welcome back!
Welcome back!

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:34.850
Charge!

00:20:35.260 --> 00:20:36.890
Wha? Huh?!

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.060
W... What's going on?

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:49.370
Merry Christmas!

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:54.140
I can't believe you all planned a
surprise party behind my back!

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:57.970
It was so obvious, we were
afraid you were going to guess.

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:00.280
Fortunately, you were typically clueless.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:04.160
From the decorations to the
food to the table settings,

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:06.630
we actually needed the cats to help out, too.

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:09.560
Thanks to them, it all went smoothly.

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:14.420
Thanks, everyone.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:19.140
By the way, Itsuki, about my
compensation for that job before...

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:22.380
All I want from you is a Christmas present.

00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:23.730
A present?

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:26.640
Spend tomorrow with me.

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:27.910
What?!

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:29.610
I was going to ask him!

00:21:29.820 --> 00:21:31.220
The race goes to the swift.

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:34.780
What?! Why are you even here?!

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:35.880
Get out!

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:37.520
Let go of him!

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:39.120
You let go!

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:44.220
That looks like fun!

00:21:46.770 --> 00:21:49.030
Help me!

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:07.820
Over and over, holding my wounded hand...
Kizutsuku te wo nandomo tsunaide

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:16.220
...you walk this uncertain path with me...
fuan bakari no kono michi wo aruite

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:29.270
...amidst the days as they slowly drift by.
yukkuri nagareta hibi no naka de bokura ga

00:22:29.540 --> 00:22:41.190
The things we obtain are so warm, so beloved.
Te ni shita mono wa konna ni atatakute itoshinda

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:47.460
Please, as time goes by, let's keep right on...
Nee konomama toki no naka

00:22:47.530 --> 00:22:51.960
...laughing and walking together.
waratte aruite yukou

00:22:52.830 --> 00:22:56.240
It's because you're with me...
Kimi ga iru kara

00:22:56.240 --> 00:23:01.330
...that I can keep moving forward.
mae ni susumerunda

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:13.210
Now our feelings are becoming one...
Ima bokura no omoi ga hitotsu ni natte

00:23:13.590 --> 00:23:17.260
...and showing the path to us.
michi wo shimesunda

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:21.490
So please, keep on holding my hand...
Dakara kono te zutto

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:25.460
...and never let it go...
hanasanaide

